\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"radio\",\"name\":\"intent\",\"value\":\"no\",\"defaultChecked\":false,\"className\":\"accent-[color:var(--accent-info)]\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"capitalize\",\"children\":\"no\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"label\",\"abstain\",{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-[--radius-md] border border-[color:var(--border-strong)] bg-[color:var(--surface)] px-3 py-1.5 text-sm has-[:checked]:border-[color:var(--accent-info)] has-[:checked]:bg-[color:var(--bg-elevated)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"radio\",\"name\":\"intent\",\"value\":\"abstain\",\"defaultChecked\":false,\"className\":\"accent-[color:var(--accent-info)]\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"capitalize\",\"children\":\"abstain\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"label\",\"undecided\",{\"className\":\"flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-[--radius-md] border border-[color:var(--border-strong)] bg-[color:var(--surface)] px-3 py-1.5 text-sm has-[:checked]:border-[color:var(--accent-info)] has-[:checked]:bg-[color:var(--bg-elevated)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"radio\",\"name\":\"intent\",\"value\":\"undecided\",\"defaultChecked\":true,\"className\":\"accent-[color:var(--accent-info)]\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"capitalize\",\"children\":\"undecided\"}]]}]],[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"ml-auto flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center\",\"children\":[\"Confidence\",[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Confidence in your vote\",\"body\":\"How firm is your decision (not how good the project is). Low = leaning this way but I could still flip after more research, conversation, or new information. Medium = comfortable with this call but open to compelling counter-arguments. High = decided, very unlikely to change. This is published next to your vote on your public DRep page so other DReps and ADA holders can read both your conclusion and how locked-in it is.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"select\",null,{\"name\":\"confidence\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"className\":\"text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"\",\"children\":\"—\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"low\",\"children\":\"Low\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"med\",\"children\":\"Medium\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"high\",\"children\":\"High\"}]]}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"checkbox\",\"name\":\"is_public\",\"defaultChecked\":false,\"className\":\"accent-[color:var(--accent-primary)]\"}],\"Publish this vote + rationale on my public DRep page\"]}],\"$L31\",\"$L32\"]}]}]]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3 flex items-center justify-between\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"Export \u0026 audit\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/proposals/hydra-2lovelaces-lidonation-cardano-mcp/export.md\",\"className\":\"rounded-[--radius-md] border border-[color:var(--border-strong)] px-3 py-1.5 font-sans text-sm hover:bg-[color:var(--bg-elevated)]\",\"children\":\"↓ Download scorecard.md\"}]]}],false]}]\n33:T24b4,{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"id\": \"hydra-2lovelaces-lidonation-cardano-mcp\",\n  \"ingestion\": {\n    \"ingested_at\": \"2026-05-11T14:30:00Z\",\n    \"ingested_by\": \"claude-opus-4.7\",\n    \"source_documents\": [\n      \"Hydra proposal page (pasted) — Proposal ID 69fbc8dd85ddd"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26899aaf207\"\n    ],\n    \"extraction_notes\": \"Notable: USD peg is $0.18, not $0.25 — most aggressive (lowest) ADA price assumption in this batch. Differs from other proposals' $0.25 peg by 28%. Audit explicitly not funded ('no additional auditing line item') and assurance is 'fully open source and open to the entire community for auditing'. Return clause exists but no contingency line is itemised in the budget breakdown — claim is 'any portion of the contingency not used' but the contingency itself isn't visible in WP totals. Proposer is two-org coalition (2 Lovelaces + Lido Nation). Total ADA is itemised as 4×WP=330K, plus 9.9K admin fee = 339,900 ADA. Smallest ask in this batch.\"\n  },\n  \"source\": {\n    \"channels\": [\n      \"hydra\"\n    ],\n    \"hydra_id\": \"69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\",\n    \"onchain_tx_hash\": null,\n    \"onchain_action_id\": null\n  },\n  \"identity\": {\n    \"title\": \"Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\",\n    \"proposer_name\": \"2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\",\n    \"proposer_type\": \"coalition\",\n    \"proposer_url\": \"https://www.lidonation.com\",\n    \"doxxed\": true,\n    \"primary_contact\": \"Emmanuel Titi (Developer Advocate); Darlington Wleh (Software Engineer, Cardano Ambassador)\",\n    \"team_size_disclosed\": null,\n    \"team_size_disclosed_note\": \"Combined '30+ years of experience'. Two named principals (Emmanuel Titi, Darlington Wleh) plus '2lovelaces' engineering team. Specific FTE count not given.\"\n  },\n  \"classification\": {\n    \"official_pillar\": \"Adoption \u0026 Utility\",\n    \"official_pillar_confidence\": \"stated\",\n    \"working_category_suggestion\": \"Tooling/DevEx\",\n    \"working_category_confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"mcp\",\n      \"ai-tooling\",\n      \"developer-experience\",\n      \"drep-tooling\",\n      \"governance-ui\",\n      \"cip-1694\",\n      \"cip-100\",\n      \"ai-agents\",\n      \"open-source\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"ask\": {\n    \"ada_amount\": 339900,\n    \"ada_amount_note\": \"Total including 9,900 ADA Intersect administration fee. Most aggressive USD peg in this batch ($0.18) — proposer claims '₳350,000 of investment' in WP4 narrative which is close to the 339,900 figure.\",\n    \"usd_amount\": 61182,\n    \"usd_peg_price\": 0.18,\n    \"pegged\": true,\n    \"currency_basis\": \"usd_pegged\",\n    \"duration_months\": 12,\n    \"milestone_count\": 4,\n    \"milestone_payments_disclosed\": true,\n    \"raw_ask_text\": \"Requested budget 339,900 ADA. USD equivalent $61,182 (ADA/USD 0.18)*. This conversion rate was specified by the proposer. Budget Summary: WP1 85,000 ADA + WP2 85,000 ADA + WP3 85,000 ADA + WP4 75,000 ADA + Intersect Budget Administration fee 9,900 ADA = 339,900 ADA total.\"\n  },\n  \"treasury_return\": {\n    \"has_return_clause\": true,\n    \"types\": [\n      \"unspent_funds\"\n    ],\n    \"expected_return_pct\": null,\n    \"expected_return_pct_note\": \"Stated return is from 'contingency not used' — but no contingency line is visible in the budget breakdown. Each WP is a single line at full value. Practical return scope unclear.\",\n    \"raw_return_text\": \"Any portion of the contingency not used will be returned to treasury.\"\n  },\n  \"lifecycle\": {\n    \"pipeline_state\": \"hydra_early\",\n    \"hydra_submitted_at\": null,\n    \"hydra_close_at\": null,\n    \"hydra_support_pct\": null,\n    \"onchain_submitted_at\": null,\n    \"onchain_vote_close_at\": null,\n    \"onchain_result\": null,\n    \"status_last_checked_at\": \"2026-05-11T14:30:00Z\"\n  },\n  \"links\": {\n    \"hydra_url\": null,\n    \"adastat_url\": null,\n    \"ipfs_cid\": null,\n    \"ipfs_gateway_url\": null,\n    \"github_url\": \"https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\",\n    \"website_url\": \"https://2lovelaces.com\",\n    \"forum_thread_url\": null,\n    \"other\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"2 Lovelaces X\",\n        \"url\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Catalyst Explorer\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.catalystexplorer.com\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"AdaLink\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.adalink.io\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Lido Nation\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.lidonation.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": {\n    \"abstract\": \"Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1," MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\",\n    \"problem_statement\": \"Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\",\n    \"proposed_solution\": \"Four sequential 3-month milestones: WP1 production engineering foundations (npm-published, CI/CD against preprod, CBOR datum decoder, security review); WP2 governance module build + developer adoption (all 54 tools live against mainnet, docs site, 3 tutorial posts, workshop, MCP registry listing); WP3 live mainnet governance validation + ecosystem integration (GovTool, Tempo.vote) + community ownership handoff (3+ external PRs merged); WP4 maintenance and close-out (active maintenance log, advocacy, close-out report and video).\",\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"@cardano-mcp/server npm package, one-command install \u003c60s\",\n      \"54 production-grade tools across 6 modules (query, transactions, tokens/NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, governance/DRep)\",\n      \"26-tool governance and DRep workbench (summarize_proposal, draft_vote_rationale, get_my_voting_queue, sentiment, forecasting)\",\n      \"CBOR datum decoder with ≥95% accuracy on real mainnet datum shapes\",\n      \"CI/CD pipeline against Blockfrost preprod\",\n      \"Documentation site with per-tool reference + 8 workflow walkthroughs\",\n      \"3 tutorial posts (UTxO queries, smart contract debugging, DRep governance)\",\n      \"Workshop recording\",\n      \"MCP registry listing at github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers\",\n      \"GovTool and Tempo.vote integration documentation\",\n      \"Live mainnet governance cycle validation report\",\n      \"3+ external contributor PRs merged\",\n      \"Close-out report and video\"\n    ],\n    \"milestones\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"WP1 (Months 1–3)\",\n        \"deliverable\": \"Production Engineering Foundations\",\n        \"ada_release\": 85000,\n        \"deadline\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"WP2 (Months 4–6)\",\n        \"deliverable\": \"Governance Module Build and Developer Adoption\",\n        \"ada_release\": 85000,\n        \"deadline\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"WP3 (Months 7–9)\",\n        \"deliverable\": \"Ecosystem Integration and Community Adoption\",\n        \"ada_release\": 85000,\n        \"deadline\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"WP4 (Months 10–12)\",\n        \"deliverable\": \"Maintenance and Close-out\",\n        \"ada_release\": 75000,\n        \"deadline\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"team\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Emmanuel Titi\",\n        \"role\": \"Developer Advocate\",\n        \"background\": \"Senior SWE / DevRel Engineer in Nairobi, Kenya. 4+ years production full-stack (TypeScript, Rust, PHP/Laravel, Vue.js, Docker, Kubernetes). Led $1M Tooling Sustainability Program at Intersect/Cardano.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Darlington Wleh\",\n        \"role\": \"Software Engineer, Co-Dreamer @lidonation, Cardano Ambassador, Co-Founder Blockchain Centre Nairobi, DB Sync Community Maintainer\",\n        \"background\": \"Deep blockchain experience across the Cardano ecosystem\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"risks_disclosed\": []\n  },\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"open_source\": \"yes\",\n    \"open_source_url\": \"https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\",\n    \"has_prior_funding\": true,\n    \"prior_funding_sources\": [\n      \"Prior funding 'As an entity, yes. For this specific work stream, no.' Specific prior grants not enumerated in this proposal.\"\n    ],\n    \"has_prior_delivery\": true,\n    \"prior_delivery_evidence\": \"W"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"orking prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp. Prior delivery: Catalyst Explorer (www.catalystexplorer.com), AdaLink (www.adalink.io). Lido Nation 'plain English, Swahili, and Spanish' educational content. Emmanuel Titi led the $1M Tooling Sustainability Program at Intersect.\",\n    \"is_administered_by_intersect\": true,\n    \"administration_fee_pct\": 3,\n    \"duplicate_of_existing_solution\": \"no\",\n    \"duplicate_notes\": \"Proposer's central claim is that Cardano has no production AI developer MCP. Worth verifying against any other in-progress MCP efforts in the Cardano ecosystem before voting. The Cardano MCP at mcp.easy1staking.com (used by this dashboard project itself) is a counter-example — but a different scope (Cardano docs vs full MCP toolkit). Multiple MCPs may coexist.\"\n  },\n  \"_meta\": {\n    \"title\": \"Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\",\n    \"proposer\": \"2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\"\n  }\n}1c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"font-sans text-xs text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"details\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer\",\"children\":[\"Raw payload · Treasury (\",\"true\",\") / Admin (\",\"—\",\")\"]}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 overflow-x-auto rounded-[--radius-md] bg-[color:var(--bg-code)] p-3 text-[11px] text-[color:var(--fg)]\",\"children\":\"$33\"}]]}]}]\n34:I[66002,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0isyf_-sk~bpm.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.~8..t7cmvyg.js\"],\"AskAiButton\"]\n22:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Proposer identity is public and verifiable.\"}]\n35:Tdbd,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quic"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"k bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Team is doxxed**\nProposer identity is public and verifiable.\n\nA doxxed team has a publicly known identity — real names, public profiles, GitHub history. Doxxing doesn't guarantee delivery, but it raises the accountability cost: a team putting their professional reputation on a proposal is harder to walk away from than an anonymous one.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident-but-wrong.23:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$35\"}]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"auto.doxxed-team\",\"value\":\"true\"}]\n25:[\"$\",\"td\",null,