n without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Prior delivery on Cardano**\nProposer has shipped previous Catalyst, treasury, or comparable work.\n\nHas this team shipped Cardano work before? Prior delivery means there's evidence — completed Catalyst projects, released software, finished reports — that they finish what they start. First-time teams aren't disqualified, but a track record is strong signal.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident…28:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"prior-delivery\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Prior delivery on Cardano\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Prior delivery on Cardano\",\"body\":\"Has this team shipped Cardano work before? Prior delivery means there's evidence — completed Catalyst projects, released software, finished reports — that they finish what they start. First-time teams aren't disqualified, but a track record is strong signal.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Proposer has shipped previous Catalyst, treasury, or comparable work.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$36\"}]}],\"$L37\"]}],\"$L38\",\"$L39\",\"$L3a\"]}]\n3b:Tdc9,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contrac"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Output is open source**\nCode, docs, or data are released under an open licence.\n\nIs the code, documentation, or data being produced released under an open licence? Open source means anyone can read, fork, audit, and reuse the work — so the value the treasury is paying for stays available to the whole ecosystem forever, not locked inside one team. Closed-source deliverables die when the team moves on.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"U…29:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"open-source\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Output is open source\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Output is open source\",\"body\":\"Is the code, documentation, or data being produced released under an open licence? Open source means anyone can read, fork, audit, and reuse the work — so the value the treasury is paying for stays available to the whole ecosystem forever, not locked inside one team. Closed-source deliverables die when the team moves on.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Code, docs, or data are released under an open licence.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\