ub.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Deliverables specific and measurable**\nOutputs are concrete, not aspirational.\n\nJudgment call: are the deliverables concrete and measurable, or aspirational and vague? Specific looks like 'three open-source SDKs published to npm with X documented endpoints by Q3'. Vague looks like 'improve the developer experience for Cardano builders'. Specific deliverables let everyone agree on whether the work was done.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side…2c:[\"$\",\"div\",\"delivery\",{\"className\":\"border-t border-[color:var(--border)]\",\"c