es, etc.). Others are human-judgment calls — value for money, public good, whether the deliverables are realistic. Those stay blank until a DRep ticks them.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3 text-[color:var(--fg)]\",\"children\":[\"Criteria can also be marked \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Not applicable\"}],\"when they don't fit the proposal — for example, \\\"open source\\\" doesn't apply to a DAO governance proposal with no software output. Those are excluded from the score entirely, neither helping nor hurting.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[color:var(--fg)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"Green requires \",80,\"% coverage.\"]}],\" If less than \",80,\"% of the applicable criteria (by points) have been answered, the verdict stays at Amber — \\\"pending review\\\" — even when every answered criterion passes. This proposal's coverage is currently \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"tabular-nums font-medium\",\"children\":[38,\"%\"]}],\" \",\"(\",7,\" of \",19,\" applicable criteria answered\",false,\").\",[\" \",\"The auto-calculated band would have been Green, but coverage is below the threshold so the verdict is shown as Amber to flag that judgment criteria are still pending.\"]]}]]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"textarea\",null,{\"name\":\"rationale_md\",\"aria-label\":\"Rationale (markdown)\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"rows\":6,\"placeholder\":\"Rationale (markdown) — this is what gets published if you toggle is_public in v2.\",\"className\":\"w-full\"}]\n32:[\"$\",\"button\",null,{\"type\":\"submit\",\"className\":\"rounded-[--radius-md] bg-[color:var(--accent-primary)] px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-[color:var(--accent-primary-strong)]\",\"children\":\"Save vote intent\"}]\n20:[\"hydra-2lovelaces-lidonation-cardano-mcp\"]\n30:[\"hydra-2lovelaces-lidonation-cardano-mcp\"]\n37:[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"auto.prior-delivery\",\"value\":\"true\"}]\n38:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[color:var(--status-green)]\",\"children\":\"✓\"}]}]\n39:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"select\",null,{\"name\":\"manual.prior-delivery\",\"aria-label\":\"Manual override for Prior delivery on Cardano\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"className\":\"text-xs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"\",\"children\":\"— inherit auto —\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"yes\",\"children\":\"✓ Yes\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"no\",\"children\":\"✗ No\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"na\",\"children\":\"🚫 Not applicable\"}]]}]}]\n3a:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":3}]\n3c:[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"auto.open-source\",\"value\":\"true\"}]\n3d:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[color:var(--status-green)]\",\"children\":\"✓\"}]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"select\",null,{\"name\":\"manual.open-source\",\"aria-label\":\"Manual override for Output is open source\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"className\":\"text-xs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"\",\"children\":\"— inherit auto —\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"yes\",\"children\":\"✓ Yes\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"no\",\"children\":\"✗ No\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"na\",\"children\":\"🚫 Not applicable\"}]]}]}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":3}]\n41:[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"auto.public-good\",\"value\":\"null\"}]\n42:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[color:var(--fg-faint)]\",\"children\":\"—\"}]}]\n43:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"select\",null,{\"name\":\"manual.public-good\",\"aria-label\":\"Manual override for Public good (benefits all of Cardano)\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"className\":\"text-xs\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"\",\"children\":\"— inherit auto —\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"yes\",\"children\":\"✓ Yes\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"no\",\"children\":\"✗ No\"}],[\"$\",\"option\",null,{\"value\":\"na\",\"children\":\"🚫 Not applicable\"}]]}]}]\n44:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":3}]\n5c:Tdc9,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Genuinely needs treasury support**\nCannot be reasonably market-funded.\n\nJudgment call: does this work genuinely need treasury funding, or could it be funded by the proposer themselves, their existing investors, or paying customers? The treasury is a finite resource — if a proposal could plausibly fund itself through normal business channels, the treasury isn't the right source.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1," public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanatio…45:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"needs-treasury-support\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Genuinely needs treasury support\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Genuinely needs treasury support\",\"body\":\"Judgment call: does this work genuinely need treasury funding, or could it be funded by the proposer themselves, their existing investors, or paying customers? The treasury is a finite resource — if a proposal could plausibly fund itself through normal business channels, the treasury isn't the right source.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Cannot be reasonably market-funded.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$5c\"}]}],\"$L5d\"]}],\"$L5e\",\"$L5f\",\"$L60\"]}]\n61:Tdc7,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, token