pe already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Aligns with the Cardano Constitution**\nPeter assesses constitutional alignment.\n\nJudgment call: does the proposal align with the Cardano Constitution's principles around governance, transparency, and decentralisation? Look for open process, accountable spending, ecosystem benefit, and no contradiction with the founding principles. The Constitution lives at constitution.cardano.org.\n# Reference: Cardano Constitution\nRead the current Constitution at:\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/IntersectMBO/cardano-constitution/refs/heads/main/cardano-constitution-2/cardano-constitution-2.txt.md\nCheck whether the proposal's stated objectives, governance model, and spending plan are consistent with the Constitution's principles — particularly around decentralisation, transparency, ecosystem benefit, and treasury s…4a:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"aligns-with-constitution\",{\"className\":\"border