g a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**USD peg is not aggressive**\nPeg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\n\nProposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims n…50:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"usd-peg-not-aggressive\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"USD peg is not aggressive\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"USD peg is not aggressive\",\"body\":"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\"Proposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Peg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$7a\"}]}],\"$L7b\"]}],\"$L7c\",\"$L7d\",\"$L7e\"]}]\n7f:Tdcd,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Treasury favourability is strong/moderate**\nAI-assigned favourability rubric — strong or moderate (not weak/none).\n\nThe return clause itself is rated strong or moderate (not weak or none). Strong means multiple substantive return mechanisms — price-peg surplus, unspent funds, revenue share — with concrete triggers and deadlines. Weak means vague promises with no enforcement.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-recor"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation r…51:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"treasury-favourability-strong\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Treasury favourability is strong/moderate\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Treasury favourability is strong/moderate\",\"body\":\"The return clause itself is rated strong or moderate (not weak or none). Strong means multiple substantive return mechanisms — price-peg surplus, unspent funds, revenue share — with concrete triggers and deadlines. Weak means vague promises with no enforcement.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"AI-assigned favourability rubric — strong or moderate (not weak/none).\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$7f\"}]}],\"$L80\"]}],\"$L81\",\"$L82\",\"$L83\"]}]\n84:Tdc7,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Has a treasury return clause**\nSurplus/unspent/revenue-share mechanism returns value to treasury.\n\nIs there a mechanism for unspent ADA, price-appreciation surplus, or revenue share to flow back to the treasury? Without one, every ADA the treasury sends is gone. With one, the proposer's incentives stay aligne"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d: if they spend less than budgeted, or ADA goes up, the treasury gets some back.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with…52:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"treasury-return-clause\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Has a treasury return clause\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Has a treasury return clause\",\"body\":\"Is there a mechanism for unspent ADA, price-appreciation surplus, or revenue share to flow back to the treasury? Without one, every ADA the treasury sends is gone. With one, the proposer's incentives stay aligned: if they spend less than budgeted, or ADA goes up, the treasury gets some back.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Surplus/unspent/revenue-share mechanism returns value to treasury.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$84\"}]}],\"$L85\"]}],\"$L86\",\"$L87\",\"$L88\"]}]\n54:[\"$\",\"input\"