rsectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, in"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"dexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Measurable on-chain KPIs**\nProposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\n\nJudgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?…58:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"measurable-onchain-kpis\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\",\"body\":\"Judgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Proposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$89\"}]}],\"$L8a\"]}],\"$L8b\",\"$L8c\",\"$L8d\"]}]\n8e:Tdb6,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/prop"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"osals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Milestone payments disclosed**\nPayment is tied to itemised milestones, not lump sum.\n\nAre payments tied to delivery milestones, or is this lump-sum upfront? Milestone payments mean the treasury releases funds as work lands. Lump-sum upfront pays in full before anything is delivered — much less leverage if the team underdelivers.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident-but-wrong.59:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"milestone-payments-disclosed\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Milestone payments disclosed\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Milestone payments disclosed\",\"body\":\"Are payments tied to delivery milestones, or is this lump-sum upfront? Milestone payments mean the treasury releases funds as work lands. Lump-sum upfront pays in full before anything is delivered — much less leverage if the team underdelivers.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Payment is tied to itemised milestones, not lump sum.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$8e\"}]}],\"$L8f\"]}],\"$L90\",\"$L91\",\"$L92\"]}]\n93:Tdcb,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The gover"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"nance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)**\nEach milestone has both an ADA amount and a target date.\n\nEach milestone has both a specific ADA amount and a target date. Less detailed schedules (amounts only, names only, none) give the proposer wiggle room. Dated amounts let everyone — proposer, DRep, community — track delivery against the plan.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident-but-wron…5a:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"milestone-schedule-detailed\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)\",\"body\":\"Each milestone has both a specific ADA amount and a target date. Less detailed schedules (amounts only, names only, none) give the proposer wiggle room. Dated amounts let everyone — proposer, DRep, community — track delivery against the plan.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Each milestone has both an ADA amount and a target date.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$93\"}]}],\"$L94\"]}],\"$L95\",\"$L96\",\"$L97\"]}]\n98:Tdc9,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Cardano MCP by Lido Nation \u0026 2 Lovelaces\nProposer: 2 Lovelaces \u0026 Lido Nation\nAbstract: Cardano is the only major blockchain without a p"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"roduction AI developer MCP. This proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation. The governance module is the proposal's defining contribution.\n\nLinks to research:\nGitHub: https://github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp\nProposer site: https://www.lidonation.com\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69fbc8dd85ddd26899aaf207\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nCardano is the only major blockchain without a production AI developer MCP. Solana has 40+. Ethereum has 30+. Every developer who tries to build on Cardano with an AI agent today gets wrong answers — and many of them quietly migrate to chains where the tooling works. This is an active driver of developer attrition that no amount of documentation, grants, or evangelism fixes on its own.\n\nThis proposal funds the production build of cardano-mcp — a working prototype already live at github.com/lidonation/Cardano-mcp — into 54 production-grade tools across six modules: query, transaction building, tokens and NFTs, smart contracts, indexing, and a 26-tool governance and DRep workbench built specifically for CIP-1694 participation.\n\nThe governance module is the proposal's defining contribution. It collapses the DRep workload — reading proposals, analyzing sentiment, forecasting ratification,…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\n**2 lovelaces and  Lido Nation**\n\nWe are Cardano enthusiasts and a growing collective of dreamers who believe in providing insightful education about Cardano in plain English, Swahili, and Spanish. Most online blockchain content is written by and for developers and finance geeks. We break down complicated technical ideas for everyday people, and provide relevant news in quick bites, and build tools that everyone can use – [https://www.lidonation.com](https://www.lidonation.com)\n\nTogether our team of creatives and engineers brings  a combined total of 30+ years of experience in product design,…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Administration model has oversight**\nIntersect-administered, or self-administered with a named oversight committee.\n\nFunds are administered with external oversight: either Intersect runs the standard milestone-gated process, or the proposer self-administers with a separately appointed Oversight Committee. 'Self-administered with no oversight' is rare and a red flag — no third party is signing off on milestones.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the…5b:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"admin-with-oversight\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Administration model has oversight\"}],[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"label\":\"Administration model has oversight\",\"body\":\"Funds are administered with external oversight: either Intersect runs the standard milestone-gated process, or the proposer self-administers with a separately appointed Oversight Committee. 'Self-administered with no oversight' is rare and a red flag — no third party is signing off on milestones.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Intersect-administered, or self-administered with a named oversight committee.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$98\"}]}],\"$L99\"]}],\"$L9a\",\"$L9b\",\"$L9c\"]}]\n5d:[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"auto.needs-treasury-support\",\"value\":\"null\"}]\n5e:[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text